            BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

 IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION OF EL PASO                            )
 ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR REVISION OF ITS RETAIL                            ) Docket No. 25-00082-UT
 ELECTRIC RATES PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE                               )
 NO. 317                                                                )

                                        BENCH REQUEST

       THIS MATTER comes before the Hearing Examiners upon El Paso Electric Company’s

(“EPE”) Amended Application for Revision of its Retail Electric Rates Pursuant to Advice Notice

No. 317 (“Amended Application”) filed on August 6, 2026.

       The Hearing Examiners issue this Bench Request to collect information to assist in their

review of EPE’s Amended Application, specifically related to EPE’s filing of its amended Rule

17.5.440 NMAC (“Rule 440”) reports.

                                          BACKGROUND

           1.   On May 7, 2026, EPE Witness George Novela filed Supplemental Testimony in

response to the Commission’s Pre-Hearing Bench Request.1

           2.   On August 6, 2026, EPE filed its Amended Application, requesting authority to

change its base rates. Specifically, among other assertions, EPE states its cost of service

demonstrates a $70.7 million non-fuel base rate revenue deficiency, reflecting a 50.5 percent non-

fuel base rate increase.2

           3.   With EPE’s Amended Application, EPE also submitted an Amended Rule 440

Filing.3




1 Supplemental Testimony of George Novela on Behalf of El Paso Electric Company (May 7, 2026).

2 Amended Application at 3.

3 EPE’s Amended Rule 440 Filing (Aug. 6, 2026).
                    BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Bench Request                                                  Docket No. 25-00082-UT


                                           DISCUSSION

       4.       The purpose of Rule 440 is for the Commission to provide guidance related to

reporting and filing requirements for investor-owned electric utilities within the jurisdiction of the

Commission. 4 Specifically, electric utilities must file reports with the Commission related to

extensions, system improvements, repairs or replacements, or additions to infrastructure.5

       5.       Prior to any request for rate recovery for such a project, a utility shall amend a Rule

440 Report to update the estimated costs, to indicate whether the estimates increased or decreased

by greater than 20 percent, and to reflect the utility’s actual costs incurred for such a project.6

       6.       To assist the Hearing Examiners in evaluating EPE’s Amended Application,

including their review and consideration of EPE’s Amended Rule 440 Filing, the Hearing

Examiners seek the following information:

                a. Pursuant to EPE Witness George Novela’s Supplemental Testimony, Exhibit
                   GN-1S, filed on May 7, 2026, EPE should verify whether the columns labeled
                   “440 Estimated Amounts” and the “Actual Amount included in Application”
                   are both for the total of EPE’s company costs, or for the New Mexico
                   jurisdictional costs.

                        i. If there is a different methodology for calculating the estimated and
                           actual costs, EPE should describe the different methodologies and
                           correct and re-file Exhibit GN-1S to clearly show the total company
                           costs and to show the total New Mexico allocated costs.

                b. Pursuant to George Novela’s Supplemental Testimony, Exhibit GN-1S, Report
                   Nos. 75 and 89 both include Project Number DN164. Project DN164 is named
                   “MOONGATE (LE1) GETAWAY & FEEDERS” in CSP-1 from EPE Witness
                   Cynthia Prieto’s Direct Testimony and “NEW 24KV AND 25KV LINE (MOO
                   23 - APO 20) FROM MOONGATE SUBSTATION TO APOLLO
                   SUBSTATION PROJECT” in Exhibit GN-1S. EPE should explain if including
                   DN164 in both 440 Report Nos. 75 and 89 is an error.


4 Rule 17.5.440.6 NMAC.

5 See Rule 17.5.440.8(A) NMAC.

6 Rule 17.5.440.8(D)(1) NMAC


                                                  -2-
                    BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Bench Request                                                  Docket No. 25-00082-UT


                c. Pursuant to George Novela’s Supplemental Testimony, Exhibit GN-1S, there
                   are eight Rule 440 Reports (Report Nos. 77, 83, 88, 101, 103, 110, 111, 114)
                   for which the difference between the estimated and actual costs exceed 20
                   percent. EPE identified these Reports in its original Application but did not
                   include them in its Amended Application. EPE should attach the updated
                   Reports to its Response to this Bench Request.

                d. The Amended Rule 440 Reports included in EPE’s Amended Application
                   contain errors and omissions. Specifically, the form labeled “NMPRC Rule
                   17.5.440 Form” was correctly filed for Report No. 70. However, for Report
                   Nos. 72, 75, 91, 92, 94, 97, 98, 99, 104, the relevant form appears to be a repeat
                   of Report No. 70. EPE should correct this error and attach the corrected
                   Amended Rule 440 Reports, including any that were omitted in EPE’s
                   Amended Application, to its Response to this Bench Request.

                e. If EPE finds any other errors, omissions, or discrepancies the Hearing
                   Examiners have not yet identified in EPE’s Amended Rule 440 Reports, EPE
                   should identify and describe such errors, omissions, or discrepancies, and attach
                   the corrected Report(s), Notices, or Testimonies to its Response to this Bench
                   Request.

       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.       On or before November 18, 2026, EPE shall file a Response which addresses the

inquiries set out in Paragraph 6 of this Bench Request.

ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on November 6, 2026.

                       NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION




